<h3>Standard formats</h3>
<h4>Date/time format</h4>
<p>
    The standart date format is <strong>yyyy-mm-dd</strong>, the standard date/time format is <strong>yyyy-mm-dd hh:mi</strong> or <strong>yyyy-mm-dd hh:mi:ss</strong>,
    where <strong>yyyy</strong> is the full year, <strong>mm</strong> is the month (1 to 12), <strong>dd</strong> is the day of the month (1 to 31),
    <strong>hh</strong> is the hour (0 to 23), <strong>mi</strong> is the minute (0 to 59), <strong>ss</strong> are the seconds (0 to 59). 
</p>
<p>
    Furtherore, there is a tooltip that shows the timezone (for example UTC +02:00 or UTC -08:00 or just UTC for the coordinated universal time).
</p>

<h4>Decimal numbers formats</h4>
<p>
    The standard decimal numbers format uses the character <strong><span id="DecimalSeparator"></span></strong> as decimal separator.
</p>
